          "prompt": "Stylized hand-painted 3D game environment art for a fast first-person roguelite shooter, matching the\nreadable visual direction of Gunfire Reborn: bold chunky silhouettes, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant\ncolour blocks, soft painted gradients and a few restrained edge accents. East-Asian desert temple fantasy. Matte stone,\nwood and cloth, restrained highlights on metal, sparse painted wear. No photorealism, micro-grain, dense tiny cracks,\nelaborate miniature carvings, harsh specular highlights or baked cast shadows. Even neutral lighting.\n\nAsset (10m wide x 11m tall x 5m deep): A monumental desert sun-temple shrine niche 10m wide, 11m tall, 5m deep that frames a magic portal: a thick sandstone facade with ONE tall open round-topped arch in the middle, 6.5m wide and 8m tall, leading into a shallow open recess 3.5m deep whose floor is flat at ground level (no steps or objects inside the recess). The recess back wall carries a large carved sun disc. The arch is edged with a gold-painted moulding and a terracotta plaster band with muted teal trim. Two stepped battered pylons flank the arch, each with one tattered vermilion cloth banner hanging flat on its FRONT face; a crenellated cornice and a small gold sun finial crown the top centre. Warm ochre sandstone, broad hand-painted planes, sparse chipped edges. The back and sides are plain closed sandstone walls.\n\nOutput: one orthographic model turnaround sheet for 3D reconstruction. Exactly four separate complete views\nof the SAME object in one row, left to right:\n1. FRONT view: the object's front faces the viewer.\n2. LEFT side view: the object turned 90 degrees so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image (camera at the\n   object's right-hand side).\n3. BACK view: the object's back faces the viewer.\n4. RIGHT side view: the object turned 90 degrees so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image.\nSame scale and same ground line in all four, each centred in its quarter with generous empty margin, never touching or\noverlapping; the whole object fits inside its quarter, nothing cropped.\nPlain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no\nperspective.",
